# Fact patterns — liability cap, Acme / Northwind

Generated from `corpus/gold/fact_patterns.jsonl` (FP-001 … FP-005). Every assertion is a
hand-computed expected value from the clause constants; the assertion is what fails if the
module drifts from the document.

> Using Legal_types as T
> Using Liability_cap_acme_northwind as L

## FP-001 — ordinary claim, before the Order Form takes effect (MSA § 9.2)

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFp001:
  output computation content L.LiabilityCap

scope TestFp001:
  definition computation equals
    output of L.LiabilityCap with {
      -- fees_paid_last_12mo: $120,000
      -- annual_fees: $240,000
      -- claim_type: T.ClaimType.Ordinary
      -- claim_date: |2026-03-01|
    }
  assertion computation.cap = $120,000
  assertion computation.uncapped = false
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope TestFp001
┌─[RESULT]─ TestFp001 ─
│ computation = LiabilityCap {
│                 -- cap: $120,000.00
│                 -- uncapped: false
│               }
└─
```

